From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Strata: the expert pyramid ladder (k helper rungs, the
 fallback rung, blob swaps)

Target: commit 1 of this series on the Seabraid compatibility patches 0001-0006 and 0010-0017 (0017: the SEABRAID_STRATA_SHM
list, seabraid_retier_blob, tier_verify, retier_check_helpers and --retier-fallback / --retier-hops).

- generate.cpp: SEABRAID_STRATA_SHM lists one channel per helper process; tier r is entry r (remote_dev kDeviceBase + r),
  Seabraid rung r + 1, fixed for the session; exit 2 when the list is malformed, has more than three entries or
  names a tier whose --expert-cache-device is unset.  --retier-promote seabraid drives every process tier (no more
  "second helper tier" refusal) and refuses an in-process GPU tier beside them; legacy modes refuse k > 1
  (retier_check_helpers).  Policy v2: ladder_boundaries 0, fallback_boundary = --retier-fallback, max_hops =
  --retier-hops; SEABRAID_PLACEMENT_QUAL is handed to the driver.  EngineHost: per-rung helper_cells, the cheap
  helper_alive (closed card / retired lease; no pid probe), after_commit(outcome) following the RAM copy only across
  the lead <-> helper 1 boundary.  open_placement: owners over k rungs + F, one RemoteRung per tier (private: tier 0
  only, phase 2), the FallbackRung.  D4 with more than one expert process exits 2 instead of picking one.
  STRATA_RAM_ADAPT / RAM_ADAPT2 with SEABRAID_STRATA_EXCLUDE_HELPER_RAM=1 skip helper-executed cells as candidates and installs.
- ownership_rungs: RemoteRung::replace sends the staged bytes (seabraid_retier_blob, kTierSwapBlob, read back by the
  helper before the ack); FallbackRung (RAM copy + pack): stage from RAM or file (counted), replace all-or-nothing,
  a RAM-resident leaving expert gives its place to the arriving one from the staged bytes, REFUSED while a RAM_ADAPT2
  read is queued for either.
- expert_source: FileExpertSource::replace_resident_from, the public face of install_resident.

Design gate: owner = the engine side of the pyramid (generate.cpp wiring, the rungs in ownership_rungs); contract =
the adapter's PlacementHost / PlacementDriver::open and the RungIO shape, nothing new on the wire; failure = exit 2 at
startup on any bad list, count, cap or mode, per-rung quarantine at run time, the fallback never closed; checker =
the adapter's host fixtures plus the live pyramid chain (FallbackRung and generate.cpp are not host-testable: they
need FileExpertSource over a real pack and main()); finish line = the live chain logs NVMe -> RAM -> h2 -> h1 -> main
and back with verified=1 on every hop.  Defenses at the sites: rung = list position (the installer maps rank to
order); D4 refused with k > 1 (no hidden rule); F leaves RAM residency of an arriving cold expert to RAM_ADAPT (one
owner of that decision).
