Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Strata: file-reference expert moves
 (--retier-file-moves), the counters and checks that go with them

Target: commit 3 of this series, on the Seabraid compatibility patches 0001-0006 and 0010-0018 (0018: FileExpertSource::file_extents,
RemoteExperts::seabraid_retier_file) and commits 1-2 of this file.

- ownership_map.hpp: RungIO::replace_from_fallback (default REFUSED: "this rung reads no files") and RungIO::reads_files(); two small
  interfaces, FileMover (one helper rung's decision) and ReadCheck (main's own read against the pack manifest), both implemented by
  the Seabraid adapter (adapters/strata/file_moves.hpp) so the rule is host-tested and this file stays free of the helper wire.
- ownership_rungs: RemoteRung forwards replace_from_fallback to its FileMover and reports reads_files() from it; its stage() asks the
  ReadCheck after copy_blob (a mismatch is REFUSED: the cell never moves, serving is unchanged).  FallbackRung::stage asks the same
  check, and counts the RAM installs that did not happen (ram_install_misses(), one WARN each) that used to be silent.
- remote_experts: seabraid_file_facts() (what the helper announced, plus its cumulative file counters); open_seabraid takes
  compact_rows.
- generate.cpp: --seabraid-compact-rows 0|1 (adapters/strata/engine_flags.hpp; default 0) now reaches the private helper launch, which
  used to hard-code it off; --retier-file-moves is the compat add-on's flag (refused without --retier-promote seabraid).  At the first
  quiet boundary open_placement stamps the pack's files, loads expert-sums.v1 ONCE (missing, malformed or stale: file moves OFF with
  one WARN, serving unchanged), gives every named helper a FileMoves over an EngineFileBackend, and hands the fallback rung the same
  read check.  EngineHost::after_round logs "helper file io: direct_bytes=N buffered_bytes=N reads=N bad_sum=N" (cumulative, summed over
  helpers; nothing when file moves are off).  TRACE handover: placement_cfg.fallback_counters is set from the FallbackRung.  REVFIX
  handover: the private tier gets set_blob_bytes(per-layer blob bytes) before its first swap, so the exact-size blob check is live.

Design gate.
  Owner    : the rule is adapters/strata/file_moves.cpp (PackSums, FileMoves); the addressing is FileExpertSource::file_extents (0018);
             the FileRef rules are the wire's file_ref_valid (run by seabraid_retier_file); the engine only answers facts.
  Contract : RungIO::replace_from_fallback + reads_files; FileMover; ReadCheck.  REFUSED always means "use bytes" and writes nothing.
  Size     : the engine side of this commit is under 260 changed lines; every new adapter file is under its header budget.
  Failure  : fail open to bytes.  Manifest missing/stale = one WARN, off.  Helper bad sum = off for that helper for the session + one
             WARN.  Main-side mismatch = ERROR, the cell keeps serving and never moves.  Timeout or torn slot = as for a blob swap.
  Checker  : adapters/strata file_moves_test, placement_file_moves_test (real runtime), engine_flags_test, placement_trace_test;
             compat retier_loop_test and test_patch_v7_commit3.py.
  Finish   : git am 0001..0018 then this mbox on STRATA_BASE; generate.cpp syntax check shows no new errors; the adapter tests pass.
             The live qualification (a GPU window) is not part of this commit.
